00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.770
MARK MIRCHANDANI: Cloud
Dataproc is a fast, easy to use,

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.750
fully managed cloud service for
running Apache Spark and Apache

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.920
Hadoop clusters in a simpler,
more cost-efficient way.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.440
Operations that used to
take hours or even days

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.570
now take seconds
or minutes instead.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:21.060
Create Cloud Dataproc clusters
quickly and resize them

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.351
at any time, so you don't
have to worry about your data

00:00:23.351 --> 00:00:25.715
pipelines outgrowing
your clusters.

00:00:25.715 --> 00:00:27.090
Dataproc doesn't
just provide you

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.650
with a Spark or Hadoop cluster.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.290
With built-in integrations
to other GCP services,

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.270
you have a powerful
and complete platform

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.552
for data processing, analytics,
and machine learning.

00:00:36.552 --> 00:00:38.760
This Qwik Start shows you
how to use the Google Cloud

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.430
Platform to create a Google
Cloud Dataproc cluster,

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.850
run a simple Apache
Spark job in the cluster,

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.800
then modify the number of
workers in the cluster.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.610
This lab is part of the
baseline Data, ML, and AI

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.460
quest on Qwiklabs Completing
